@page "/examples/render-modes"
@* No @rendermode: this page is statically rendered and hosts interactive islands. *@

<ExampleHeader Title="Render modes" Level="Complex" Mode="Static SSR + Server & WebAssembly islands">
    The same component in five islands. Islands share a bus only when they share a DI container, which is
    the boundary documented in <code>docs/events/design/render-modes.md</code>.
</ExampleHeader>

<StaticStateReader />

<div class="row g-3 mt-1">
    <div class="col-lg-6">
        <h2 class="h5">Interactive Server: one circuit, one bus</h2>
        <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
            <IslandPanel Name="Server A" @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
            <IslandPanel Name="Server B" @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
            <EventScope Name="static-scope">
                @* This EventScope is rendered statically. Its cascade can't cross into the island,
                   so island E ends up on the circuit's root bus, the same one A and B use. *@
                <IslandPanel Name="Server E (inside a static EventScope)" @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
            </EventScope>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
        <h2 class="h5">Interactive WebAssembly: one runtime, one bus</h2>
        <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
            <IslandPanel Name="WASM C" @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
            <IslandPanel Name="WASM D" @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<HowItWorks>
    <p><strong>Try it:</strong> increment and ping from each island. Wait for the WebAssembly islands to become interactive first.</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>A, B and E share</strong> a count and pings: every Interactive Server island on a page lives in the same circuit, so they resolve the same Scoped <code>IBus</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>C and D share</strong> with each other: all WebAssembly islands share one runtime and one DI container (the client <code>Program.cs</code> calls <code>AddBlazorBus</code> too).</li>
        <li><strong>Server and WebAssembly islands never share.</strong> They're different DI containers. The library deliberately has no JS bridge (ADR-007).</li>
        <li><strong>E shows the cascade caveat.</strong> An <code>EventScope</code> declared in static markup doesn't reach an island inside it. Declare scopes <em>inside</em> interactive components.</li>
        <li>The static reader at the top got a value from the request's own throwaway bus. Static and prerendered components read state but never subscribe.</li>
    </ul>
</HowItWorks>
